        "lead": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>We started Estates Liquor in November 2025 for one reason: the bottles worth chasing had become almost impossible to buy at a fair price.</p>",
            "style": "lead"
          }
        },
        "body_1": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Allocated bourbon arrives in small quantities and disappears fast. Somewhere between the distillery and the shelf, that scarcity turned into a game — lotteries, waitlists, bundles you did not want attached to the one bottle you did, and secondary-market pricing dressed up as retail.</p>",
            "style": "body"
          }
        },
        "body_2": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>We are not a discount outlet, and we do not chase every commodity brand. <strong>Bourbon is our core focus</strong>, alongside rare tequila, wine, and premium spirits worth the shelf space. When an allocated bottle lands, we list it at fair retail that day. No lottery. No waitlist to buy in.</p>",
            "style": "body"
          }
        }
